## Interface: 120100
## Title: MoxieTracker
## Notes: Displays current character Artisan Moxie, Shard of Dundun, Unalloyed Abundance, and Fused Vitality, plus per-character Knowledge Points and Concentration rosters, in three movable windows.
## Author: Tharavol
## Version: @project-version@
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\inv_10_gearcraft_artisansmettle_color2
## Category: Professions
## SavedVariables: MoxieTrackerDB

## X-ReleaseNotes: Shows the current character's Artisan Moxie, Shard of Dundun, Unalloyed Abundance and Fused Vitality in a compact panel docked to the top-right of the crafting window, appearing automatically when that window opens and hiding again when it closes. Moxie is tracked for all eleven professions, and rows appear only for the professions the character actually has; Shard of Dundun, Unalloyed Abundance and Fused Vitality always show even at zero. Currencies are matched by ID rather than by name, so the addon works on any client locale, and Fused Vitality is counted across bags, bank and reagent bank. Each count is coloured against its own thresholds - Shard of Dundun green at 6 and red at 7-8, Unalloyed Abundance green at 800 or more, Moxie green at 600 or more, Fused Vitality green at 20 or more, yellow otherwise - and hovering a line shows the same tooltip as the default currency UI. Any row can be hidden from the options panel. A second window lists unspent profession Knowledge for every character that has logged in, name in white and a per-profession breakdown in green indented beneath it, building up automatically as you play each character; a character with nothing unspent is left off the list. A third window tracks Crafter's Concentration the same way, with a projected time until each profession reaches its cap that keeps counting even for an offline character. All three windows are independently movable and remember their own positions from the options panel; each of the two roster windows can mute individual characters or just one of their professions, and either window can be turned off entirely. The order characters are listed in, shared by both rosters, defaults to alphabetical and can be customized with Up/Down buttons on its own options page; a character not yet placed in a custom order is appended alphabetically after the ones that are. Configure under Options > AddOns > MoxieTracker or with /moxie (alias /moxietracker); /moxie help lists every command. Source, issues and release notes: https://github.com/Tharavol/MoxieTracker

